{
  "body": "The delivered redesign gives Review and Verify meaningful stored explanation fields that callers can select, edit and render directly. Summary and assessment scope explain the conclusion and its limits; rationale and limitations retain complete actor-authored reasons. Verify changes describes delivery. Existing structured judgments, findings, actors, subjects and evidence retain their factual authority. Rendering derives readable output from selected values without introducing another body or interpreting old prose.\n\nComplete assessments and narrow whole-field updates share closed validation, revision conflicts, source-byte preservation and transaction recovery. V3 Review findings retain stable IDs with editable current accounts; v2 findings and change-level blockers preserve their original basis. Explicit applicability and responsible reassessment remain separate from storage success. Recognized review.set and verify.set use valid schema-3 responses even before a store is validated, while the original schema-2 operation contract remains intact.\n\nThe assessed scope includes the complete local engineering diff, coordinated owner models/examples, approved Delivery allocation, CLI/schema/validator behavior, canonical skill consumers and generated-package compatibility. Current independent Design and whole-change Code Review, together with the referenced final evidence, support reliance on the delivered subjects. The original Proposal approval retains its earlier meaning; the explicit user revision to v3 finding immutability and its current Design assessment govern that scoped refinement. All required corrections were independently dispositioned before this separate Verify.\n\nNew stores use rigorloop-records-v3. Existing v2 work, including this initiative, continues under its original complete contract without migration. This report intentionally uses that existing v2 representation. Required local tests, integrated public-command proof, candidate CI and package checks cover the affected boundaries. The referenced evidence explains exact commands, results, candidate identities, traceability and why its engineering basis remains current despite subsequent review/workflow recording.\n\nLimits and recovery: no hosted CI, remote PR creation, merge, release, publication or customer-adoption result is claimed. Publication prerequisites remain separately owned. Existing-v2 retirement requires a separate decision; historical records are not converted. After a real v3 store exists, rollback must retain a compatible executable and recovery access rather than down-converting records. The normalized Git basis below supports only the assessed local branch handoff; PR must revalidate remote identities and exercise the user's separate submission authorization.\n\nverification_basis:\n  repository_identity: github.com/xiongxianfei/rigorloop\n  remote_identity: https://github.com/xiongxianfei/rigorloop\n  base_branch: main\n  base_revision: d670788c894ccdfb7eec5f973b61bdc964dd52a1\n  merge_base_revision: d670788c894ccdfb7eec5f973b61bdc964dd52a1\n  head_branch: proposal/structured-assessment-explanations\n  verified_subject_revision: 602b9d2f7aba477b106f182b75477a3cb5b5cc25\n",
  "change_id": "2026-09-10-structured-assessment-explanations",
